<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:wp81="using:Cornflower.Themes.Wp81">
  <!--
    The Windows Phone 8.1 ContentControl: the default style of the 8.1 Update 1 runtime (contentcontrol.json, which
    equals the SDK's generic.xaml), re-expressed as an Avalonia ControlTheme. docs/controls/ContentControl/PLAN.md
    has the values and their sources.

    The phone's style sets two values, HorizontalContentAlignment Left and VerticalContentAlignment Top, and a
    template of one part: a ContentPresenter placed by them, so the content sits at the top left at its own size,
    inside the control's Padding (the presenter's Margin). The template draws nothing of its own: no Background, no
    BorderBrush, no BorderThickness, so a ContentControl given them draws none, as on the phone. It has no states.

    The text Avalonia's presenter makes of data gets the phone's 1.33 em line (PhoneHeaderLine): a WinRT
    ContentControl doesn't recognise access keys, and nor does this one.

    Every ContentControl wears it, as on the phone: the theme keyed by type below is based on the keyed one, which a
    template can also set by name.

      <ContentControl Theme="{DynamicResource Wp81ContentControlTheme}" />

    A ContentControl in the template of a control Wp81 doesn't theme yet (the managed file dialog, and Simple's
    DataValidationErrors in its Simple TextBoxes) keeps Avalonia's own, as under Simple alone: HoleParts.FallBack, and
    HoleParts.FallBackToOwn, as Simple has no ContentControl theme to fall back to. An app that hosts its pages in a
    ContentControl sets both content alignments to Stretch, as the phone's Frame has them (frame.json).
  -->
  <ControlTheme x:Key="Wp81ContentControlTheme" TargetType="ContentControl">
    <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Left" />
    <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Top" />
    <Setter Property="Template">
      <ControlTemplate>
        <ContentPresenter x:Name="PART_ContentPresenter"
                          Margin="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                          HorizontalAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                          VerticalAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                          Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                          ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                          wp81:PhoneHeaderLine.IsEnabled="True" />
      </ControlTemplate>
    </Setter>
  </ControlTheme>

  <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type ContentControl}" TargetType="ContentControl" BasedOn="{StaticResource Wp81ContentControlTheme}">
    <Setter Property="wp81:HoleParts.FallBackToOwn" Value="True" />
    <Setter Property="wp81:HoleParts.FallBack" Value="True" />
  </ControlTheme>
</ResourceDictionary>
